Warning: spoilers ahead:







I mean it, serious spoilers ahead







An athame can be used to enscribe Elbereth
without dulling ever.  Picking things up
and casting spells from an Elbereth erases
part of the Elbereth.

Athame messages can't be written over, but 
wands of cancellation and turn invisible cause
the writing to vanish.

On food:
floating eyes give telepathy
black unicorns are GREAT sacrifices to Neutral Gods
blue jellies can give heat, cold and poison resist.
Leprechauns give teleportation
tengus give teleport and teleport control
quantum mechs give and remove speed, 
("your velocity is uncertain, more you are moving faster")
invisible stalkers give invisiblity and see invisible, but
you may have to quaff of potion of invisibility and 
confusion for them to be permanent.
gray dragon scale mail gives magic resistence, so
you can wear a cloak of, say, displacement.
A stethoscope is useful in the endgame because the 
Wizard keeps showing up after you killed him and doesn't
always show up in human form.
This way, you can keep track of the # of levels you've
drained from him with your Stormbringer or vampire form.
master lichs are fun forms for polymorph fiends, they
have a -4 AC, 17 HD cause frost when they hit and don't
burst out of armor, I think they also regenerate.
Don't recall if they drain levels, cause slow occasionally.
I intend to test out demiliches (sp?) sometime.
blessed potions of gain level keep giving hit points and
mana even after level 30.
Dragons that are fun to eat: Black disintergrate resist
                             Blue lightning
                             Orange sleep
                             White, cold, Red flame.
Grays don't give magic resistance by eating, nor yellows
acid.  Greens may give poison resistence but it may be 
academic at that point.... ;*) ;*)
The drawbridge can be brought down with a knock spell.
Simple to get into the castle now.
cursed scrolls of create monster can summon about 20
monsters, say, minotaurs, with wands, or dwarf kings,
with pickaxes, weapons and armor.  You get to choose
what monsters appear show you could summon ten giants
and ten wraith or so.  Love them rings of conflict!
Some chests blow up doing electrical damage, destroying
wands and rings, (maybe amulets too, never checked) drop
these before opening chests.
chameleons cause you to change, but its not permanent, at
least, it wasn't the time I ate one.
